# Bran Underhill - scout of the missing Wayfarer party, found holed up in the
# border ruin (Act 1, quest 1). Points the player to the campsite; optionally
# joins the party.
# Compile with:  scripts\Compile-Dialogue.ps1

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_Bran

entry joined if in_party()
entry camp_return if flag(TSC_BranAtCamp)
entry pointed if flag(TSC_BranPointedCamp)

== start ==
A voice from the rubble, first: "That's far enough, friend."

Then a broad-shouldered man steps out from behind a fallen beam, longsword raised, gambeson patched in six places. He looks you over, taking in the road dust and the guild seal on your letter, and lowers the blade with relief.

"The Guild sent you? Eight weeks, and they finally send somebody. Bran Underhill, Serra Voss's scout. Before you ask: the company's alive. Or was, twelve days ago, when the raiders cut me off from camp."

* "Twelve days? What happened out here?" -> story
* "The rubble tells a story. Rationed fires and a single bedroll. You're here alone." -> read_ruin
    if not flag(TSC_BranRead)
    check Investigation 6 -> read_ruin | read_miss
* "The guild wants you found. Where's the rest of your company?" -> point_camp
* "You look like you could use a road partner, Bran." -> offer

== read_ruin ==
Bran's eyebrows climb. It's the first thing about you that's genuinely surprised him.

"Aye." He looks at the ruin with new eyes, seeing what you saw. "Twelve days holed up and the first person I see reads my whole camp. The guild sent the right rider."

* "Then give me the short version: where's your company?" -> point_camp
    do flag(TSC_BranRead); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)
* "Habit. What happened out here?" -> story
    do flag(TSC_BranRead); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)

== read_miss ==
"...Rationed fires?" Bran glances at the fire-blackened corner where he has plainly been burning whole logs at once. "Friend, I've been cooking rats over a bonfire for twelve days. Good instinct, wrong ruin."

* "Fair enough. What *did* happen out here?" -> story

== story ==
"Same thing that happens to everything out here. We cornered the thing we've been hunting, and the pass surprised us. Raiders on the roads and our last raven eaten by a hawk."

He sits on a fallen block, suddenly tired.

"I was scouting a route to the cave when the raiders pushed between me and camp. Been living in this ruin since, eating scraps."

* "Cornered *what*, exactly?" -> quarry
    do flag(TSC_BranStory)
* "Where's the rest of the company?" -> point_camp
    do flag(TSC_BranStory)
* "Come with me. We'll sort it together." -> offer
    do flag(TSC_BranStory)

== quarry ==
Bran glances around the ruin from habit (there's nobody for kilometers) and lowers his voice anyway.

"Serra will want to tell it proper. But you've earned a taste: we've been stalking an ettersnap. Yes, they're real. Ask at the camp."

* "Then point me at the camp." -> point_camp
* "You're coming too, surely." -> offer

== point_camp ==
Bran pulls a strip of bark from his sleeve, scratched over with a scout's shorthand, and marks your map with a burnt twig.

"The camp's here. Half a day, if the raiders let you keep your boots. Serra and Oswin will be there, gods willing. Tell them Bran's alive and the eastern route is watched."

* "Marked. Now, come with me, Bran." -> offer
    do flag(TSC_BranPointedCamp); signal(TSC_Quest1_WayfarersCall, TSC_BranFound); give_quest(TSC_Act1_Camp)
* "I'll carry the word. Hold fast, Bran." -> held_fast
    do flag(TSC_BranPointedCamp); signal(TSC_Quest1_WayfarersCall, TSC_BranFound); give_quest(TSC_Act1_Camp)

== held_fast ==
Bran nods slowly and settles back against the stones, sword across his knees.

"Held fast is what I do. I'll give the raiders a few days to find something else worth their attention, then work my way back to camp the long way around. If I'm there before you, I'll tell Serra you're coming."

He tips his chin at the road you rode in on.

"And you watch yourself, courier. The bandits hold the low road now. If you see smoke bigger than a cookfire, ride wide of it."

* "I'll keep my eyes open. Stay safe." -> end
* "Save the warning. I'm the thing on that road worth fearing." -> end

== offer ==
"With you?" He looks at the ruin, then at his sword's worn edge, then at you.

"I've eaten rat and nettle soup for twelve days and named a wall Gerald. You know what? Yes. Point me at the road. Serra can shout at me for getting cut off when we're all around the same fire."

* "Welcome aboard, Bran." -> welcomed
    do join_party(); affinity(+5)
* "Actually, hold the ruin a while longer." -> held_fast
    do affinity(-5)

== welcomed ==
Bran shoulders his pack like it weighs nothing, whistles once through his teeth, and spits on the ruin's threshold.

"Kept your watch, Gerald. Somebody else's turn."

He falls in beside you. For the first time, he grins.

"Right. Camp's half a day out. I'll show you the best route. If we run into the raiders, we'll have better odds together."

* "Let's move." -> end
    if flag(TSC_BranPointedCamp)
* "First, mark the camp for me." -> point_camp
    if not flag(TSC_BranPointedCamp)

== pointed ==
Bran looks up from running a whetstone along his sword.

"Still here. The low road's still crawling, so camp will have to wait a few days more. You know where it is: half a day out, and mind the bandits on the way. Standing ready if you've changed your mind about company."

* "I have. Come with me, Bran." -> welcomed
* "Just passing through." -> end

# He kept his word: left at the ruin, he slipped past the raiders and walked
# back to camp on his own. Still recruitable here, with camp-appropriate lines.
== camp_return ==
Bran sits mending the firepit's stack, gambeson over his knees and the longsword within reach out of pure habit. He grins when he sees you.

"Told you I'd manage. Gave the low road two nights to get bored of me, then came over the ridgeline. Serra shouted for a while. It was almost good to hear."

* "Glad you made it, Bran. Come with me; the road's not done with us." -> camp_join
* "Any trouble on the way in?" -> camp_road
* "Good to see you by a proper fire."

== camp_road ==
"Some. The bandits have pushed pickets right up the low road, like they're waiting for something worth stealing to come along." He looks at you meaningfully.

"That's you, courier. Whatever you're carrying out of these hills by the end, they'll want it. Worth remembering."

* "Then I could use a sword that knows the area. Join me." -> camp_join
* "I'll remember. Rest easy, Bran."

== camp_join ==
Bran looks over at Serra's tent, then back at you, and there's no twelve days of rat in the decision this time.

"Aye. The company's fed and back on its feet; it's you walking into the dark places alone. Point me at the road."

He takes up the longsword and falls in beside you.

* "Welcome aboard, Bran."
    do join_party(); affinity(+5)

== joined ==
Bran checks the edge on his knife with a thumb.

"Standing ready. Where's the road taking us?"

* "Teach me to hold a line the way you do, Bran." -> warden_teaching
    if flag(TSC_BranLoyal) and not flag(TSC_BranTaught)
* "Anything on your mind, old watchman?" -> confidant
    if affinity(>=15) and not flag(TSC_BranConfided)
* "Serra is riding with us now, Bran. Hesk." -> serra_time
    if flag(TSC_BranCellarSeen) and in_party(TSC_Npc_Serra) and not flag(TSC_BranSerraTold)
* "Carry on, Bran."

# The other half of the cellar: he decided at the ruin whether Serra gets
# told, and she does not join the company until Act 5, so the decision sits
# with the player for two acts before it can be acted on.
== serra_time ==
Bran looks over at the fire, where Serra is doing something unhurried to a bowstring.

"Aye," he says. "I have been finding reasons for a week. They are all good reasons and not one of them is the reason."

* "Then go." -> serra_go
    if flag(TSC_BranTellSerra)
* "You said when you were ready." -> serra_wait
    if not flag(TSC_BranTellSerra)

== serra_go ==
He stands up before he can talk himself out of it, and does not look back to see if anybody is following.

* [Go with him.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_BranSerraPending)

== serra_wait ==
"I did. I said that." He turns the knife over. "Ask me again. Keep asking me. Ready is not a thing I am going to arrive at on my own."

* "I will keep asking." -> end
    do flag(TSC_BranTellSerra); affinity(+5)

== confidant ==
Bran considers the road behind you both before he answers.

"Only that forty years of Underhills stood a wall and watched the kingdom rot past it. And the first time I walk *away* from a post, the road hands me a company worth keeping." He taps his knife's pommel twice, an old watch signal. "All quiet. That's the report."

* "All quiet. Carry on, Bran." -> end
    do flag(TSC_BranConfided); grant_xp(10)

== warden_teaching ==
Bran looks you over the way he looked over the ruin's walls, checking for the weak courses.

"The watch had a saying: anyone can swing steel, but standing still when everything around you says run, that's a trade." He unbuckles his gambeson and tosses it to you. "Put that on. We start with how to take a hit."

The rest of the day is bruises, footwork, and the hard small rules of shields. By nightfall, your stance has changed.

* [Learn the Warden's trade] "Again tomorrow, Bran." -> end
    if not flag(TSC_BranTaught)
    do flag(TSC_BranTaught); learn_class(TSC_Class_Warden); grant_xp(25)
* "Another time. The road beckons." -> end
